      "lastReply": "A young tiger named Raja lived deep in the forest, where he spent his days hunting and napping under banyan trees. One evening, the wind carried the most incredible smell from a nearby village—spices, rice, and something magical he had never tasted. Curious, he crept closer and watched through a window as a grandmother stirred a huge pot of biryani, layering rice and meat with care.\n\nRaja decided he had to learn this art. The next day, he approached the grandmother's house and, in his gentlest voice, asked if she would teach him. She was startled at first, but saw the earnest hope in his eyes and agreed. For weeks, Raja practiced—chopping onions with his claws, toasting spices without burning them, and learning the patience needed to let the biryani steam just right.\n\nFinally, the day came when Raja cooked his first perfect pot. He invited all the forest animals to a feast under the stars. As they ate together, the tiger realised that the best part was not the biryani itself, but the joy of sharing something he had made with his own paws. From that day on, Raja became known as the forest's finest cook, and his biryani brought everyone together. 🐅🍛\n\n6:57 PM",
